\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Distribution of the criterion fraction $\mathrm  {CF}$ across the primary $4{,}410$-cell $(r, V, v)$ sweep at the headline cell $(N, d'_{\max }, f_0, h) = (4,\, 2,\, 0.5,\, \sqrt  {}\,)$ under the inherited independence assumption $\rho = 0$, per conservation variant. Quantiles are over the $n = 2{,}205$ valid cells per variant. The inherited paper reports $\mathrm  {CF}\in [0.60, 0.96]$; the true range is wider on both ends. Values from \texttt  {Rebuild/sims/C1--cf-distribution/output/results.json} (rb-003; output sha256 \texttt  {91fc4692\ldots  }), block \texttt  {summaries.variant\_A/rho\_0.0} and \texttt  {summaries.variant\_B/rho\_0.0}.}}{11}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
