\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Cell-wise paired comparison $\Delta \mathrm  {CF}:= \mathrm  {CF}(\rho {=}0.2) - \mathrm  {CF}(\rho {=}0)$ across the $4{,}410$-cell sweep, per variant. ``Flat'' uses tolerance $|\Delta \mathrm  {CF}| \le 10^{-5}$. The variant-A pattern is a one-sided ordering ($84\%$ of cells decrease in $\rho $). The variant-B pattern is mixed-sign ($64\%$ decrease, $24\%$ increase, $13\%$ flat), generalising the rb-002 headline-cell observation that variant-B $\mathrm  {CF}$ is essentially flat in $\rho $. Block-keys \texttt  {delta\_distribution.<variant>}.}}{16}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
