\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Iso-VDA contour band over the experimental-design plane $(V, v)$ for the rebuilt model at the headline cell $(N, d'_{\max }, f_0, h) = (4,\,2,\,0.5,\,\sqrt  {}\,)$, variant~A. Rows: cross-location correlation $\rho \in \{0,\, 0.2\}$ (top: inherited independent model; bottom: with the A1 decorrelation channel of Section~\ref {sec:model} at the Cohen--Maunsell~\cite  {CohenMaunsell2009} V4 anchor $r_{SC} \approx 0.2$). Columns: benefit/cost asymmetry $r\in \{0.3,\, 1,\, 3\}$ (cost-dominant, symmetric, benefit-dominant). The vertical reference $V= 1/N= 0.25$ is the chance baseline; the $v= 1$ row is the value-blind reference where $\mathrm  {VDA}\equiv 0$ by construction. Filled contours are at $\mathrm  {VDA}\in \{0,\,0.001,\,0.005,\,0.01,\,0.025,\,0.05,\,0.1,\,0.15,\,0.2\}$ on a common scale. The band shape replaces the inherited §4 ``narrow regime'' description and §5.2 categorical claim with a quantitative boundary the reader can compute pointwise. Reproduced from \texttt  {Rebuild/sims/C3--iso-vda-Vv/output/figures/iso\_vda\_contours.png} (rb-010; output sha256 \texttt  {72820559\ldots  }).}}{20}{figure.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:iso-vda-contours}{{12}{20}{Iso-VDA contour band over the experimental-design plane $(\valid , \val )$ for the rebuilt model at the headline cell $(\Nloc , \dprimemax , f_0, h) = (4,\,2,\,0.5,\,\sqrt {}\,)$, variant~A. Rows: cross-location correlation $\corr \in \{0,\, 0.2\}$ (top: inherited independent model; bottom: with the A1 decorrelation channel of Section~\ref {sec:model} at the Cohen--Maunsell~\cite {CohenMaunsell2009} V4 anchor $r_{SC} \approx 0.2$). Columns: benefit/cost asymmetry $\Rsens \in \{0.3,\, 1,\, 3\}$ (cost-dominant, symmetric, benefit-dominant). The vertical reference $\valid = 1/\Nloc = 0.25$ is the chance baseline; the $\val = 1$ row is the value-blind reference where $\VDA \equiv 0$ by construction. Filled contours are at $\VDA \in \{0,\,0.001,\,0.005,\,0.01,\,0.025,\,0.05,\,0.1,\,0.15,\,0.2\}$ on a common scale. The band shape replaces the inherited §4 ``narrow regime'' description and §5.2 categorical claim with a quantitative boundary the reader can compute pointwise. Reproduced from \texttt {Rebuild/sims/C3--iso-vda-Vv/output/figures/iso\_vda\_contours.png} (rb-010; output sha256 \texttt {72820559\ldots })}{figure.12}{}}
