\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces C2 conservation-family band on the peak of $\mathrm  {VDA}(r)$ at the headline cell ($N= 4$, $V= 0.5$, $d'_{\max }= 2$, $f_0 = 0.5$, $h = \sqrt  {\cdot }$, $\rho = 0$, variant~A). Per $(v, p)$: $r^*$ = argmax of $\mathrm  {VDA}(r)$ on the rb-006 $84$-point log-$r$ grid; $\mathrm  {VDA}^*$ = the corresponding peak height. The peak height moves systematically with the conservation order $p$ (band $+14\%$ at $v= 5$); the peak location $r^*$ is grid-discretely stable at large $v$. Source: \texttt  {Rebuild/sims/A3--conservation-band/}\allowbreak  \texttt  {output/results.json} \texttt  {block\_A\_peaks}; sha256~\texttt  {055bf4ec\ldots  }.}}{32}{table.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:a3-c2-peak-band}{{15}{32}{C2 conservation-family band on the peak of $\VDA (\Rsens )$ at the headline cell ($\Nloc = 4$, $\valid = 0.5$, $\dprimemax = 2$, $f_0 = 0.5$, $h = \sqrt {\cdot }$, $\corr = 0$, variant~A). Per $(\val , p)$: $\Rsens ^*$ = argmax of $\VDA (\Rsens )$ on the rb-006 $84$-point log-$\Rsens $ grid; $\VDA ^*$ = the corresponding peak height. The peak height moves systematically with the conservation order $p$ (band $+14\%$ at $\val = 5$); the peak location $\Rsens ^*$ is grid-discretely stable at large $\val $. Source: \texttt {Rebuild/sims/A3--conservation-band/}\allowbreak \texttt {output/results.json} \texttt {block\_A\_peaks}; sha256~\texttt {055bf4ec\ldots }}{table.15}{}}
